## Data and environment

| Concern | Approach |
|---|---|
| Database | Containers (Testcontainers) or a per-run schema; run migrations first |
| Isolation | Transaction rollback or truncate per test |
| External APIs | Stub with nock or MSW in Node |
| Time and randomness | Inject clock and id generator |
| Parallelism | One database or schema per worker |

## Common mistakes

- Calling `app.listen` in the module under test, causing port conflicts.
- Sharing mutable state across tests.
- Asserting only status codes, not error body shape that clients depend on.
- Mocking the database so heavily that queries are never exercised.

Both offer auto-waiting, network interception, screenshots and CI support. Details change between releases, so **verify current documentation**.

| Aspect | Playwright | Cypress |
|---|---|---|
| Architecture | Controls browser through protocol, out of process | Runs in the browser with a Node helper |
| Browsers | Chromium, Firefox, WebKit | Chromium family, Firefox; WebKit experimental (check current status) |
| Multi-tab, multi-origin | Native, via contexts and pages | Improved over time, with constraints |
| Parallelism | Built in, with sharding | Parallelisation commonly via paid dashboard or CI splitting |
| Languages | TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Java, .NET | JavaScript, TypeScript |
| Debugging | Trace viewer, inspector, codegen | Interactive runner, time travel |
| Component testing | Available (experimental in some versions) | Mature component testing |

